As we only defined the Hub and Spoke VNETs (with their subnets), but we haven't deployed the Azure firewall yet in to the Azure Firewall Subnet - 
so we will deploy that in the Hub Spoke VNET. Azure deploys the firewall using a standard name: AzureFirewallSubnet and 
is defined privately - 10.0.0.4 /26.
The /26 gives Azure enough IP addresses for the firewall's infrastructure.

You shouldn't put VMs, application servers, or other resources in that subnet
